&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;mso-ansi-language: EN-US;&quot;&gt;The Demand Planner is responsible for ensuring supply alignment to meet customer demand while maintaining healthy inventory levels. This role serves as the primary planning interface across cross-functional teams, driving forecast accuracy, optimizing supply utilization, and supporting business growth through data-driven planning processes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;mso-ansi-language: EN-US;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;mso-ansi-language: EN-US;&quot;&gt;What will you do?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;mso-ansi-language: EN-US;&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Challenge and validate commercial assumptions through trend analysis, historical performance, market insights, and demand signals.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Promote a One Number culture through the adoption of Integrated Business Planning (IBP) best practices and data-driven decision-making.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Monitor and improve key planning KPIs, including Forecast Accuracy, Bias, Fill Rate, Inventory Health, Excess &amp;amp; Obsolete Inventory, Aging Inventory, and Months on Hand (MOH).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Support the digitalization of planning processes through advanced analytics, automation, and reporting tools.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Approve, release, and monitor the status of production and purchase requisitions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Develop priorities and communicate with support functions while taking an active role in problem resolution as required.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Coordinate with Sales, Supply Chain, Logistics, and Operations teams to ensure optimal inventory levels and maximize customer fulfillment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Regularly update work order due dates based on fluctuations in internal capacity and factory delivery schedules.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Keep the Supply Chain &amp;amp; Logistics Manager informed of any changes affecting production or procurement lead times to ensure planning data remains accurate and up to date.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Regularly monitor and update safety stock levels in the system as needed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identify opportunities to improve current planning processes and recommend corrective actions and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;mso-ansi-language: EN-US;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
