&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Midea America Corp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Midea America Corp. is a U.S. subsidiary within Midea Group, the Fortune 500 giant known for making life easier for millions around the globe. As the world&amp;rsquo;s top maker of home appliances, Midea is proud of its 166,000+ employees and presence in 200+ countries, including here in the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Parsippany, N.J., with an innovation hub in Louisville, Kentucky, Midea America provides practical innovations that surprise and delight, creating moments to cherish at home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Midea&#x27;s lineup of appliances - from refrigerators to air conditioners, laundry solutions and floor care - are high quality, reliable, and affordable. By thoughtfully engineering performance, convenience, and design into every product, Midea delivers on the promise of every appliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we expand our footprint in the United States, we seek a US IP Attorney to strengthen our intellectual property protection and strategy. This position will oversee Midea&amp;rsquo;s intellectual property matters in the United States, including patent prosecution, IP litigation, licensing, and enforcement. The role involves collaborating with global R&amp;amp;D teams, outside counsel, and business units to ensure the company&amp;rsquo;s innovations are adequately protected and aligned with business objectives. This position is preferred to be based in Louisville, KY, but we may also open to Parsippany, NJ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patent Strategy &amp;amp; Prosecution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a US patent strategy aligned with Midea&amp;rsquo;s global IP portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the preparation, filing, and prosecution of US patent applications in collaboration with outside counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct freedom-to-operate (FTO) analysis, patentability assessments, and prior art searches for new product developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance to engineering, R&amp;amp;D, and product teams on patent strategies and IP risk mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IP Litigation &amp;amp; Enforcement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee IP litigation and disputes in the US, including patent infringement lawsuits and ITC Section 337 investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with external counsel on legal proceedings and pre-litigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop enforcement programs against counterfeit products, unauthorized use of Midea&amp;rsquo;s IP, and trade secret misappropriation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor competitors&amp;rsquo; IP activities and provide risk assessments to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licensing &amp;amp; IP Transactions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and negotiate IP licensing agreements, technology transfer deals, and strategic partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and draft joint development agreements, NDAs, and collaboration contracts involving IP rights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct IP due diligence in M&amp;amp;A transactions and business partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trademark &amp;amp; Brand Protection&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the branding and marketing teams to register, enforce, and protect Midea&amp;rsquo;s trademarks in the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Address trademark oppositions, domain name disputes, and brand misuse cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Training&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with US patent, copyright, and trade secret laws, as well as industry regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver IP training programs for R&amp;amp;D, engineering, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated on legal developments in US IP law and advise the company on regulatory changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor (JD) degree from an accredited US law school.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Admission to a state bar (preferably California, Texas, or New York).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;USPTO registration required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of IP experience in a law firm or in-house legal department, with a focus on patents, trademarks, and IP litigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of US patent laws, USPTO procedures, and IP litigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with engineering and R&amp;amp;D teams, particularly in consumer electronics, appliances, or manufacturing industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage outside counsel and legal budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent negotiation, analytical, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating with global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mandarin proficiency is a plus but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
