&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Midea America Corp:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Midea America Corp. is one of the world&amp;rsquo;s largest home appliance brands, offering the most comprehensive selection of products in the world to fully serve the needs of day-to-day living at home, at work, or anywhere else you go. In North America we strive to aim high, put the customer first, transform, and innovate the marketplace, utilizing our commitment, dedication, inclusion, and partnership with our teams. We are a global company with over 150,000 employees and operations in more than 195 countries. As a publicly listed company, we are also ranked #245 as a Fortune Global 500 company and offer one of the most comprehensive ranges in the home appliance industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This new position will lead all product safety and field return activities for the Small Appliances team. The ideal candidate will have 10+ years of R&amp;amp;D and product safety experience, preferably in consumer products/appliances segments. This candidate will work closely with the R&amp;amp;D teams regarding product safety &amp;ndash; including field surveillance, root cause analysis, product safety training, and third-party safety regulatory requirements (i.e. UL, CSA, etc.).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Job Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor reports of safety allegations from multiple streams of data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a new and improved database system to track all reported safety allegations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a new field return lab to investigate product safety allegations related to all small appliances and environmental products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the quality organization to determine which units to return to the lab for further evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external forensic investigators, on allegations associated with property damage beyond the product, to understand the narrative of the event and findings from both scene and lab exams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to third party lab and/or scene exams as needed to investigate safety allegations resulting in property damage, to determine cause and origin of the event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summarize and report out findings from all streams of data on a monthly and/or ad hoc basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights and feedback to R&amp;amp;D team regarding construction and testing requirements for future products under development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a champion to further establish and define product safety processes and procedures for the team to follow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product safety training for an international team of engineers on an annual basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers regarding product safety best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage various action items &amp;amp; day-to-day communication with various internal/external parties &amp;ndash; including local engineering team, international teams, legal department, investigators, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a thorough understanding of existing and upcoming safety regulation changes affecting these products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the R&amp;amp;D teams to ensure future compliance &amp;amp; that the necessary design work is being achieved to meet regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a hands-on engineer who can work in the lab to test units and root cause failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain excellent communication with global colleagues &amp;ndash; including taking occasional weekend/evening calls or meetings, helping track project milestones, deliverables, action items, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel domestically &amp;amp; internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&amp;rsquo;s degree in engineering, preferably Mechanical Engineering or Electrical Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years&amp;rsquo; engineering experience, preferably in consumer electronics/appliances segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience investigating insurance claims &amp;amp; failure modes specific to small appliances, fans, heaters and air purifiers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of heater recall constructions and failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of arc tracking failure modes and experience testing PCB designs to limit the propagation of such failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A general understanding &amp;amp; familiarity with the construction of heaters, electric pressure cookers, air fryers and other small appliances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting forced failure testing, including NiCr wire, locked rotor, and UL flammability testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Goal-oriented &amp;amp; self-managed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication &amp;amp; organization skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a collaborative team-environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a self-starter with excellent organization skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&amp;rsquo;s degree in engineering, preferably Mechanical Engineering or Electrical Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct product safety experience in consumer electronics/appliances/HVAC segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified Fire &amp;amp; Explosion Investigator (CFEI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EPA 608 certified&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of working with global colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Midea America Corp. is one of the world&amp;rsquo;s largest home appliance brands, offering the most comprehensive selection of products in the world to fully serve the needs of day-to-day living at home, at work, or anywhere else you go. In North America we strive to aim high, put the customer first, transform and innovate the marketplace, utilizing our commitment, dedication, inclusion and partnership with our teams. We are a global company with over 150,000 employees and operations in more than 195 countries. As a publicly listed company, we are also ranked #245 as a Fortune Global 500 company and offers one of the most comprehensive ranges in the home appliance industry. Midea America is a subsidiary of Midea Group with over 200 employees in the US and we are expanding our presence in North America. Know more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nBc_5XKM6MM&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Midea Group&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location : Plano, Tx;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job Responsibility:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serving as the &quot;Technical Hub&quot; for the North American regional business team, this role deeply supports business breakthroughs and project deliveries for strategic accounts. You will be responsible for the end-to-end technical alignment from pre-sales solution design to project delivery, ensuring solution competitiveness and high-quality implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Core Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. Pre-sales Solution Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Key Account Managers (KAMs) to deeply explore the technical requirements of strategic clients; deliver customized data center solutions encompassing magnetic bearing chillers, fan walls, liquid cooling CDUs (Cooling Distribution Units), intelligent building control systems, and energy efficiency optimization modules across multiple technical pathways (air, water, and liquid cooling).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsible for drafting technical proposals during project bidding, conducting thermodynamic and energy efficiency simulations, performing solution reviews, and calculating cost estimates to ensure both the technical feasibility and commercial viability of solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Act as the primary technical interface for clients, leading technical exchanges, site surveys, and solution demonstrations to build technical trust with clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Project Delivery &amp;amp; Technical Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge the gap between sales and EPC/engineering teams to ensure a smooth transition from solution design to the delivery phase; participate in the review of construction plans and the implementation of technical standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coordinate internal and external resources (headquarters&#x27; product teams, supply chain, and engineering subcontractors) to resolve critical technical challenges and perform root-cause analysis (RCA) for failures during delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support the setup and testing of client POC (Proof of Concept) environments to ensure technical metrics meet client requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3. Product &amp;amp; Capability Building&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gather North American market requirements and competitor dynamics to feed back to headquarters&#x27; Product Managers, actively participating in product roadmap and certification planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and enrich the regional solution knowledge base for North America, compiling typical case studies and best practices to empower the regional team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirement:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. Experience &amp;amp; Background&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Education: Bachelor&amp;rsquo;s degree or above, majoring in Refrigeration and Cryogenic Engineering, Thermal Energy and Power Engineering, HVAC (Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning), or related fields.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Industry Experience: 8+ years of data center-related experience, with a background spanning solution design, project delivery, or technical support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Project Track Record: Experience in successfully implementing overseas (specifically North American) data center projects is highly preferred; familiar with international standards such as Uptime Tier and TIA-942.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Professional Skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;System Expertise: Proficient in data center infrastructure systems, with a deep understanding of the coupled relationships between cooling systems, IT loads, power supply/distribution, and building automation; candidates with a full-stack technical perspective are highly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Selection: Familiar with data center product portfolios, system architectures, and equipment selection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bidding &amp;amp; Risk Management: Proven capability in drafting technical proposals, calculating cost estimates, and managing project risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sustainability Insights: Knowledge of low-carbon, energy-saving data center technologies (liquid cooling, modular designs, etc.) is a strong plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial Acumen: Able to independently conduct financial calculations for TCO, Capex, and Opex, with the ability to justify technical choices through the lens of client financial metrics and economic value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3. Core Competencies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Language &amp;amp; Presentation: Professional working proficiency in English, with excellent cross-cultural communication and presentation skills; capable of engaging in direct, deep technical alignments and debates with overseas clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Resilience: Outstanding cross-functional collaboration skills (interfacing with Sales, Product, and Engineering teams); able to respond rapidly to client demands in high-pressure environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
