&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: 15.0pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &#x27;Segoe UI&#x27;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &#x27;Times New Roman&#x27;; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none; mso-fareast-language: ZH-CN;&quot;&gt;The Dishwasher Technical Product Engineering Manager supports the development and strategic direction of built-in, portable, and compact dishwasher platforms for the US market. This role is a key member of the R&amp;amp;D team, responsible for driving innovation, evaluating product quality, and collaborating with internal and international teams to design differentiated dishwashing solutions and advance product performance, efficiency, and user experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: 15.0pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &#x27;Segoe UI&#x27;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &#x27;Times New Roman&#x27;; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none; mso-fareast-language: ZH-CN;&quot;&gt;This position is full-time and fully on-site. Some domestic and international travel is required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: 15.0pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: &#x27;Segoe UI&#x27;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &#x27;Times New Roman&#x27;; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none; mso-fareast-language: ZH-CN;&quot;&gt;Supervisory Responsibilities:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
