&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Solutions engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Midea America&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Midea America Corp. is a U.S. subsidiary within Midea Group, the Fortune 500 giant known for making life easier for millions around the globe. As the world&amp;rsquo;s top maker of home appliances, Midea is proud of its 166,000+ employees and presence in 200+ countries, including here in the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Parsippany, N.J., with an innovation hub in Louisville, Kentucky, Midea America is dedicated to providing practical innovations that surprise and delight, creating moments to cherish at home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Midea&#x27;s lineup of appliances - from refrigerators to air conditioners, laundry solutions and floor care - are high quality, reliable, and affordable. By thoughtfully engineering performance, convenience, and design into every product, Midea delivers on the promise of every appliance to make your life a little easier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Provide pre-sales technical support for key overseas data center accounts, and work closely with KAMs to drive major customers, key projects, and strategic opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Understand customer requirements in depth and support technical communication, solution matching, product selection, configuration recommendations, and technical clarification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Provide technical support for both primary-side and secondary-side cooling products, including chillers, air-cooled solutions, liquid cooling CDUs, fan walls, and precision air conditioning applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Participate in customer presentations, bid support, technical proposal preparation, customer Q&amp;amp;A, and technical coordination with consultants and EPC partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Understand core data center requirements in areas such as power density, redundancy level, energy efficiency, liquid/air cooling ratio, and reliability, and support the development of customer-facing solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Coordinate with product, R&amp;amp;D, delivery, and after-sales teams to ensure smooth collaboration from pre-sales support through project execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Summarize standard solutions, typical application cases, and competitor technical information based on project experience to support platform business expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Bachelor&amp;rsquo;s degree or above, preferably in HVAC, Refrigeration and Cryogenic Engineering,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Energy and Power Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Automation, Mechatronics, or related fields.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; At least 3 years of technical support experience in data centers, HVAC, central cooling plants, liquid cooling, or related industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Familiar with data center cooling system architecture, including air cooling, water cooling, liquid cooling, and free cooling solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Candidates with knowledge of high-density racks, AI data centers, liquid cooling infrastructure, and GPU clusters are preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Able to independently conduct customer requirement analysis, technical solution preparation, technical communication, and basic product/system selection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Strong communication, presentation, and cross-functional coordination skills, with the ability to work effectively with sales, product, delivery, and customer technical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; English can be used as a working language for customer communication, technical documentation, and cross-regional collaboration; overseas local hire or willingness to travel internationally is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Experience in Hyperscaler, Colo, AI data center, or ICT infrastructure projects is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Experience in supporting integrated primary-side and secondary-side solutions is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Experience working with consultants, EPC contractors, general contractors, or large system integrators is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Experience in liquid cooling, CDU, fan wall, precision air conditioning, or large-scale cooling plant applications is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package, to learn more, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &#x27;Aptos&#x27;,sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: &#x27;Times New Roman&#x27;; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;&quot;&gt;Careers Page (midea.com)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Midea America Corp. is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Midea America Corp. is one of the world&amp;rsquo;s largest home appliance brands, offering the most comprehensive selection of products in the world to fully serve the needs of day-to-day living at home, at work, or anywhere else you go. In North America we strive to aim high, put the customer first, transform and innovate the marketplace, utilizing our commitment, dedication, inclusion and partnership with our teams. We are a global company with over 150,000 employees and operations in more than 195 countries. As a publicly listed company, we are also ranked #245 as a Fortune Global 500 company and offers one of the most comprehensive ranges in the home appliance industry. Midea America is a subsidiary of Midea with over 200 employees in the US and we are expanding our presence in North America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Plano, TX&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are searching for a skilled and experienced Compressor Test Engineer to join our team. As a Test Engineer, you will be supporting the Plano Compressor Lab by executing test protocols on the compressor Calorimeter and Psychrometric Chamber, analyzing performance data, generating engineering reports, and assisting in our compressor lab, ensuring the smooth operation of equipment and testing processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also be supporting customer field visits, providing technical support to our customers on our compressor products. This will include troubleshooting issues, performing repairs, writing test reports, and offering service as needed to ensure optimal customer satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity for someone with a strong engineering background who has a passion for compressors, HVAC, is practical, hardworking, and energetic, and is willing to get his hands dirty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person is willing to get trained in HVAC, compressors, calorimeters, and HVAC system testing in the Psychrometric chamber using AHRI 210/240 &amp;amp; ASHRAE 37 test method.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run/Supervise the compressor Calorimeter, Psychrometric room HVAC testing, and compressor teardown and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct on-site visits to assist customers with issues, installation procedures, advising on maintenance, and repairs of compressor equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the sales team to ensure accurate product information and technical specifications are provided to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong relationships with customers, providing ongoing support and ensuring their needs are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with technicians to execute laboratory tests and experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and maintain compressor test and gaging equipment, and ensure all components are functioning properly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform inspections, calibrations, and troubleshoot equipment malfunctions as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and analyze data from tests and experiments, and make reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise and analyze teardown compressors and generate a failure report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inventory of equipment and spare parts, and coordinate maintenance and repairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain lab protocols and procedures, and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Midea America Corp is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A Warehousing Specialist at MIDEA is responsible for overseeing and optimizing warehouse operations, ensuring accurate and efficient storage, handling, and distribution of goods. This role involves inventory management, process improvement, and compliance with safety and quality standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Inventory Management: Monitor and maintain inventory accuracy on a daily basis through regular audits and cycle counts. Ensure proper storage and labeling of products to facilitate efficient retrieval and distribution. Coordinate with procurement and sales teams to manage stock levels and minimize shortages or excess inventory.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Warehouse Operations: Planning and organizing warehouse layout and workflow to optimize space utilization and operational efficiency. Implement and maintain warehouse organization and cleanliness, and manage material transfers between different warehouses.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Shipping and Receiving: Coordinate incoming and outgoing shipments, ensuring timely and accurate processing of orders and deliveries.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Safety and Compliance: Ensure compliance with health and safety regulations in the warehouse environment, conducting routine inspections to maintain operational safety and equipment functionality. Also train warehouse staff on best practices and safety protocols.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Technology Utilization: Manage ERP system activities (material entries and location changes).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Customer Service: Collaborate with other departments to ensure timely fulfillment of customer orders and address any warehouse-related customer inquiries or issues.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reporting and Documentation: Maintain accurate records of shipments, inventory movements, and warehouse activities. Prepare reports on inventory levels, order fulfillment, and warehouse performance metrics.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Among other duties as assigned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What are we looking for?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; 1+ years of experience in warehousing, inventory control, or logistics.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Proficiency in warehouse management systems (WMS) and Microsoft Office Suite.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bachelor&#x27;s degree in International Business, Industrial Engineering or related field.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Basic English.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge, Skills, Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Inventory Management: Understanding inventory control methods, including First In, First Out and Just-In-Time, to ensure optimal stock levels and minimize carrying costs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Warehouse Operations: Knowledge of warehouse layout optimization, space utilization techniques, and workflow management to maximize efficiency and productivity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Logistics and Supply Chain: Familiarity with logistics processes, transportation modes, and supply chain principles to coordinate inbound and outbound shipments effectively.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Safety and Regulatory Compliance: Awareness of warehouse safety regulations and best practices to maintain a safe working environment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Warehouse Management Systems: Proficiency in using software to track inventory, manage orders, and streamline warehouse operations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Problem Solving and Decision Making: Ability to analyze data, identify issues or inefficiencies in warehouse operations, and implement effective solutions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Customer Focus: Understanding the importance of meeting customer requirements and ensuring timely and accurate order fulfillment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Communication and Collaboration: Strong communication skills to coordinate with internal departments (such as procurement, sales, and customer service) and external stakeholders (suppliers, logistics providers) to achieve operational goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal Traits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Organizational Skills: Strong organizational abilities to manage multiple tasks, prioritize workload, and ensure that deadlines and goals are met efficiently.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Problem-Solving Aptitude: A proactive approach to identifying challenges within warehouse operations and implementing effective solutions. This involves critical thinking, analytical skills, and the ability to think on your feet.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adaptability: Flexibility to adapt to changing circumstances, such as fluctuations in demand, unexpected supply chain disruptions, or evolving business priorities.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Team Orientation: A collaborative mindset to work effectively with diverse teams, promoting a positive work environment, and fostering teamwork and cooperation among warehouse staff.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Integrity and Ethics: Upholding high ethical standards in all interactions and decisions, including maintaining confidentiality when handling sensitive information.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Attention to Detail: Thoroughness in overseeing inventory accuracy, quality control, and adherence to safety protocols to ensure operational excellence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resilience: The ability to remain calm and composed under pressure, navigate challenges, and maintain productivity during peak periods or unforeseen circumstances.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Continuous Learning: A willingness to stay updated with industry trends, technological advancements in warehouse management systems, and best practices to continuously improve warehouse operations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-motivated and Comfortable in Dynamic, Fast-Moving Organization: Demonstrates initiative and adaptability in a rapidly changing environment, ensuring consistent performance and responsiveness to evolving demands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull; Monday to Friday schedule.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Opportunity to be part of a global, fast-growing company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
